# =============================================================================
# DB CAPABILITY CONTRACT — single declared database capability (thirtieth-audit
# item 28). Every environment that chooses a PostgreSQL product MUST consume
# exactly the image pinned below — never a different database product.
#
# Declared capability
# -------------------
#   PostgreSQL major      : 16 (PG_MAJOR)
#   Image (pinned)        : PG_IMAGE — pgvector/pgvector:pg16 (includes the
#                           PostgreSQL 16 server + the pgvector extension).
#                           Dockerfile reference: github.com/pgvector/pgvector
#                           docker/16/Dockerfile (this tag's multi-arch index
#                           digest is pinned below, so the reference is
#                           immutable across every consumer).
#   Required extensions   : vector, uuid-ossp, pgcrypto, pg_trgm
#                           (migration 004_rfq_quote_tables.sql requires
#                           CREATE EXTENSION vector — plain postgres:16 images
#                           CANNOT satisfy the contract, which is why E2E and
#                           every other environment must use PG_IMAGE).
#   Required features     : pg16 row-level security (FORCE RLS), SQLx
#                           migration ledger (_sqlx_migrations), JSONB, GIN
#                           indexes, trusted extensions (initdb creates them
#                           as the bootstrap superuser before migrations run).
#
# Who consumes what (each entry MUST carry the exact PG_IMAGE literal; the
# enforcement script scripts/validate-db-contract.sh fails CI on drift):
#   env                       file(s)                                        role
#   ------------------------  ---------------------------------------------  -------
#   DB contract CI            .github/workflows/db-contract.yml              fresh-DB + least-privilege/RLS + clean-bootstrap gates (2 service containers)
#   E2E browser release gate  .github/workflows/e2e-playwright.yml           Playwright E2E against a real migrated DB (1 service container)
#   Rust CI (unit/integration) .github/workflows/sensei-rs-ci.yml            test + integration + security service containers (3)
#   CD pre-flight             .github/workflows/cd.yml                       test + integration service containers (2)
#   Local dev Compose         docker-compose.yml                             db + integration-db services
#   Production Compose        docker-compose.prod.yml                        db + bootstrap + grants services
#   Kubernetes chart          k8s/helm/sensei/values.yaml                    database.imagePin (production DB must be provisioned from this image
#                                                                             family; the bundled Bitnami subchart is dev/eval only and CANNOT
#                                                                             satisfy the vector requirement)
#
# Bump procedure: update PG_IMAGE below (new tag and/or digest), then update
# every literal in the consumer files to match — the validator enforces the
# equality, so CI will fail until all consumers are repinned together.
# =============================================================================
PG_MAJOR=16
PG_IMAGE=pgvector/pgvector:pg16@sha256:ccc6e83d6e35e931dc7c5def2022729d5a6c370318d099181995567ff1fb4d6b
PG_REQUIRED_EXTENSIONS=vector uuid-ossp pgcrypto pg_trgm
